  "note": "An archived pre-temporal production build is compared with the current default temporal-radius build (icpTemporal omitted) in independent worker contexts. The archived control predates the temporal diagnostics, normalized to disabled/zero for validation; an explicit false request also isolates any compatible baseline. Both explicitly select scalar leaves (icpSimd:false) and retain the unchanged ICP reference/tree/lazy-normal cache under its existing 128 MiB capacity budget. An archived scalar production build supplies an excluded exact result/PLY oracle. Every call loads a fresh unchanged full measured moving cloud before timing. Previous-iteration slots live only within each call; no moving result or cross-call correspondences are reused. One excluded first-use pair, five excluded alternating warm-up pairs, ten alternating timed pairs unless overridden. Every current pair requires identical transform/RMS/iterations/convergence and all transformed PLY bytes, equal cache capacities and expected reuse/bounds flags. Temporal diagnostics must show positive tighter-radius query counts and exactly four bytes per sampled point (at most 200000 bytes), released before return. A tighter radius is not a branch-saving count. Whole RPC includes correspondence search, overlap selection, lazy normals, matrix accumulation/solve, transform application and output indexing. Normal KNN and full point-to-plane matrix are unchanged. Loading/pool startup, exports, validation and removal excluded. First-use samples are not cold medians. Input/manifest/original measured source/seven implementation sources/script/current and archived production builds hashed before/after. No builds/tests/scans during timing. CPU clocks/power/GC/other apps uncontrolled; even/odd measured-source subsets are not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. No GPU adapter/model metadata collected."
